   "t": "Денис, это моя мама.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Denis, this is my mom.' The grammar packs 'Denis' and 'mom' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Мама, это мой парень Денис.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Mom, this is my boyfriend Denis.' The meaning hinges on 'mom' working together with 'Denis' in spoken Russian. Eleonora answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Мне очень приятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Very nice to meet you.' In Russian, the idea of 'to me' flows naturally into 'pleasant' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Не бойся, мама не кусается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do not be afraid, Mom does not bite.' Katya anchors the line on 'not', while 'bites' completes the thought.",
